# Information

Information is framed as a mental model — a conceptual tool for navigating complexity through patterns and relationships. It draws on four source traditions: personal knowledge management (Tiago Forte, Sönke Ahrens), systems thinking (Kevin Kelly), and critical thinking (Rolf Dobelli).

## Key Sources
- [[building-a-second-brain---tiago-forte]]
- [[how-to-take-smart-notes---snke-ahrens]]
- [[out-of-control---kevin-kelly]]
- [[the-art-of-thinking-clearly---rolf-dobelli]]

## Definition
Information is a mental shortcut or framework for making sense of patterns and relationships in complex situations. It positions information not merely as data or facts, but as an active navigational principle.

## Confidence
0.7 — definitional/modeling exercise rather than empirical evidence.